{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793468749,"nonce":"4NHuc7RunxBMyxVx1WaOh7TEDDc=","message":"Heaps preview smoothness, committed in f9a866e and 989145d. Added: build cache keyed on a hash of the compiler, hxml files, class-path sources, libraries and the shim (about 9 s first launch, 2 s unchanged); app name as the tab and header label; credit pacing (CREDIT viewer to app, ACK app to viewer, at most 2 outstanding; an app that never sees a credit keeps its 60 fps timer); a live header readout (fps shown, frames per second from the app, tick interval, credits per second and outstanding, ticks without a new picture). Measured on a quiet Mac: with credits every frame is shown once (58 shown, 58 from the app, 58 credits/s, 0 outstanding), and a fake viewer granting 60 credits/s got 60.0 frames/s with a frame gap of median 17.0 ms and p95 18.1 ms. The remaining unevenness is on the presentation side: the viewer's frame loop waits in CAMetalLayer nextDrawable (1576 of 1769 main-thread samples), frames take 16 to 28 ms under Fifo because ashui configures frame latency 1; immediate mode gives steady 9 to 16 ms ticks but no display sync and still looked skippy. A near 1:1 picture size (RAYDE_SURFACE_SIZE=1600x1200) looked smoother than 800x600 scaled 2.1x, so the doubled look was mostly resampling. Next: ashui 6e22681 (frame latency 2 as an app setting and ASHUI_FRAME_LATENCY), then re-measure; draw the app at the tab's pixel size (needs a resize record in the protocol); fiber-aware reads in Ash (050ee14) or a poll-based native pipe; viewer timestamps in credits so the app's frame time is exact. Not done: OpenFL, Flixel, Lime and Ceramic producers; hosted previews through the session; Linux and Windows hdlls.","files":null}]}